cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below (and cite the original paper too)."
title: "A proof of Conjecture A.1 of Liu-Wu-Zhang-Zhou, with all-parameter sharpness and a Lean 4 proof"
abstract: >-
  A proof of Conjecture A.1 proposed in Appendix A of Liu-Wu-Zhang-Zhou,
  Comm. Math. Phys. 375 (2020) 785-832. Over every characteristic-zero field,
  let X,Y be linear endomorphisms of any vector space and Z = XY - YX satisfy
  XZ = ZX and YZ = ZY. For all natural p,q and vectors v, the hypotheses
  X^{p+1}v = Y^{q+1}v = 0 imply (X+Y)^{2p+2q+1}v = 0.
  The repository includes a complete Lean 4 proof of this original statement,
  an all-parameter written tensor construction proving sharpness, technical
  notes, and finite exact rational-arithmetic checks. The sharpness construction
  is not itself formalized in Lean.
